 "notes": "All figures from Note 10 of the FY2025 10-K; FY2023 identical to the FY2023 10-K (no restatement). Amazon allocates all operating expenses to its three segments, so 'other' is zero. The 10-K describes North America and International as retail sales of consumer products (incl. from sellers), advertising and subscription services through online and physical stores (physical stores explicitly mentioned only for North America); AWS as compute, storage, database and other services. Devices (Kindle, Fire TV, Echo, Ring, Blink, eero), Alexa, Prime Video and Twitch are named in the 10-K at company level but not assigned to a specific segment, so they are not listed as segment brands. 2025 operating income includes a $2.5bn FTC settlement (North America) and ~$2.7bn severance (all segments). Segment arithmetic checks exactly."
